{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: Browser identity, onboarding and authorized import. Implementation work package 4 of the reviewed connected-story design (planning b5f1fb3f, exact Draft2 evidence209a5ec9, approvalfc77cf82 and adopted direction0f358e52). Source baseline e6e6782 and the active acts/MCP a199 composition are context, not approval; reconcile current reviewed main, relevant existing requests and ecbc722a runner changes before editing.\n\nScope and decisions:\nImplement browser identity/device panels and create/join/import onboarding in the existing UI/client/hosted Worker. Each supported browser stores its own non-extractable Ed25519 CryptoKey in IndexedDB with room IDs and device metadata; test actual browser support and storage-clear recovery. Another device generates another key and joins the same active member through existing admin-authorized, short-lived, single-use client-custody invitation. The fragment secret authorizes redemption; current invitations do not bind a chosen key fingerprint before redemption. Device labels/fingerprints are informative, not authority. Non-admin enrollment/removal asks an admin initially; self-service and bound-key pairing are later contract work.\nImplement short authenticated read-session renewal, task discovery from current member authority, revoked-session/watch termination, admin revocation, same-active-member lost-key recovery through another admin and the existing offline recovery key. Founding setup offers offline recovery material and a second device; no remaining admin/recovery authority means there is no current same-member recovery path. Never impersonate a member using email, site sign-in or operator access.\nConnect initial public GitHub import to a browser broker that creates an isolated Artifacts copy; also support an operator-approved existing Artifacts identity. Reuse lane J founding and existing policy bootstrap a13a0bf5: show explicit policy choice/digest, persist founding/join/import attempt identity before sending and reconcile lost replies/unknown provider effects without creating duplicates. A source URL is not an Artifacts identity. Grant R-GEN-12 onboarding authority only after authenticating the authorized founding attempt. Define and enforce broker authentication/rate limits/cleanup. Private-source OAuth, mirroring and other providers can follow.\nApply the reconciled design decisions, not Draft1 wording: existing sessions are read-only; controls use signed resource/action-bound current owner/admin requests. Initially one new agent member and one DO/conversation/lane per task; no in-place owner reassignment. Last-active-owner-key revocation or owner removal stops new tools/broker writes/renewals; another active owner device keeps independent-agent work alive. Admins retain private export/settlement, and lost-key recovery restores only an active member, never a removed handle. Optional delegated agent mode is not required in initial runtime delivery; its key-bound grantor rules and conditional acceptance remain specified. Render repository/command output inert in the key-owning origin and expose only minimal activity to other Room readers.\nPrivate-read contract decision carried from independent revised-design review: initial raw owner/admin resources require a direct device read session, whose direct-key provenance and current role/resource are verified by the trusted Room boundary. authenticateRead returning an owner/admin member handle is insufficient. Deny delegation-issued read sessions raw resources by default; any separately scoped private-read capability is later explicit contract work. Sessions stay read-only, and controls remain separately signed.\n\nDependencies and order:\nRequired relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b538c5eace50a1de82a8bdf8a8f19764548af15e. Reviewed shared authority/access contract; existing roster/session/invitation/founding contract; lane J and a13a0bf5 policy bootstrap reused, not duplicated. Reconcile source at current reviewed acts/UI composition and budget settings. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.\n\nAcceptance outcome:\nA new browser creates/joins a real Room, saves its device key and imports a real supported repository with explicit initial policy and understandable progress/failure/retry states, without a local CLI. Lost join/found/import replies recover one room/member/repository. Device B enrolls as the same member and discovers A's ongoing task; an uninvited browser and used/expired invitation are refused. Revoking A stops its old access while B retains authority; separate independent-agent work remains available. Recover the same member with another admin and with offline recovery authority; no-authority and last-admin failures are clear. A removed handle is clearly unrecoverable; no silent invitation/role reset restores it. Show owner-last-key and owner-removal stops separately from ordinary device loss and revocation with another active key.\n\nValidation:\nKnown existing runners: npm run typecheck; npm test --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui; npm run test:node --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-client; npm run e2e --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui. Choose focused identity/onboarding files and one compact browser boundary with two separate profiles, then the final retained gate at delivered head. Record actual commands after current test-runner/source reconciliation; no repeated whole-repo setup.\n\nDelivery: use an isolated request branch/worktree, record promise and exact source/probe evidence, publish every changed path at the exact delivered head, and obtain independent normal review before integration. Source code/protocol amendments are not authorized by the evidence-only design verdict alone. No numerical test inventory/per-guard sweep, no new first-Jam readiness gate. If a provider/storage/authority mechanism cannot meet the stated story, report a design discrepancy rather than silently reducing scope.","body":{"conditions":"A new browser creates/joins a real Room, saves its device key and imports a real supported repository with explicit initial policy and understandable progress/failure/retry states, without a local CLI. Lost join/found/import replies recover one room/member/repository. Device B enrolls as the same member and discovers A's ongoing task; an uninvited browser and used/expired invitation are refused. Revoking A stops its old access while B retains authority; separate independent-agent work remains available. Recover the same member with another admin and with offline recovery authority; no-authority and last-admin failures are clear. A removed handle is clearly unrecoverable; no silent invitation/role reset restores it. Show owner-last-key and owner-removal stops separately from ordinary device loss and revocation with another active key. Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b538c5eace50a1de82a8bdf8a8f19764548af15e. Relevant contract decisions and exact implementation evidence independently reviewed; source artifacts integrated through normal landing. Preserve named lifecycle/authority/durability rules and existing owed work. Known existing runners: npm run typecheck; npm test --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui; npm run test:node --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-client; npm run e2e --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-ui. Choose focused identity/onboarding files and one compact browser boundary with two separate profiles, then the final retained gate at delivered head. Record actual commands after current test-runner/source reconciliation; no repeated whole-repo setup.","dependencies":"Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b538c5eace50a1de82a8bdf8a8f19764548af15e. Reviewed shared authority/access contract; existing roster/session/invitation/founding contract; lane J and a13a0bf5 policy bootstrap reused, not duplicated. Reconcile source at current reviewed acts/UI composition and budget settings. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.","priority":"After highest-priority test-overhead ecbc722a; preserve acts/Jam-blocker/Jam-and-docs order. No new first-Jam gate.","target_head":"e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}